    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Boxing The Compass is Haircut One Hundred’s first album since Pelican West, marking a notable return for the band after decades away from a full-length studio statement. Released on October Is Orange, it presents the group in a renewed form while retaining the bright, melodic pop sensibility that made their early-1980s breakthrough so distinctive.\n\nMusically, the album is rooted in pop-rock with a strong funk foundation, a combination that has long been central to Haircut One Hundred’s appeal. Reviews of the record highlight airy vocals, clean guitar lines, and upbeat rhythmic drive, suggesting a band that has kept its catchy, sunlit style while framing it as a “complete change in direction” in the sense of the title’s nautical phrase. The set includes 10 new songs, among them “Come Back to Me,” “Vanishing Point,” and “A Wonderful Life,” and it has been presented as a comeback record that reconnects with the sound of the group’s classic era.",
